(GRM-17: the expr precedence chain - expr ::= or_expr, or_expr ::=
 and_expr ("or" and_expr)*, and_expr ::= comparison ("and" comparison)*,
 comparison ::= additive (comp_op additive)*, additive ::= multiplicative
 ((add|subtract) multiplicative)*, multiplicative ::= primary
 ((multiply|times|divide|modulo) primary)*. All six levels exercised in
 one expression: {2 add 3 multiply 4} is 14 (additive/multiplicative
 nested inside a comparison) and {5 subtract 1} is 4 (a second
 comparison) joined by "and", then "or false" at the top. multiply binds
 tighter than add (2 add 3 multiply 4 = 14, not 20), matching the grammar.
 IMPORTANT: this only parses inside a condition position (an `If`), NOT
 as a var_decl/assignment/print initializer - see Discrepancy 1
 (cross-ref EXP-D3, expressions.md) - the Grammar Summary's own `expr`
 production is used, unqualified, by var_decl/assignment/print_stmt, but
 the compiler only accepts a `comparison` there when nothing else in the
 sentence has already claimed "is" as a copula/assignment verb.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox GRM-17.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   chain holds
)
If 2 add 3 multiply 4 is 14 and 5 subtract 1 is 4 or false, print "chain holds".
